'''Visa requirements for British citizens''' are administrative entry restrictions by the authorities of other states placed on citizens of the [[United Kingdom]].

As of 2026, [[British nationality law|British citizens]] have visa-free or visa on arrival access to 184 countries and territories, ranking the [[British passport]] 6th in the world according to the [[Henley & Partners Passport Index|Henley Passport Index]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.henleyglobal.com/passport-index/ranking |title=Global Passport Ranking - The Henley Passport Index |website=Henleyglobal.com |date=2025 |access-date=23 January 2025}}</ref>

The United Kingdom left the European Union on 31 January 2020, and British citizens consequently lost their freedom of movement to EU countries; however, under the [[Common Travel Area]], British citizens continue to have freedom of movement to Ireland.

Visa requirements for other classes of [[United Kingdom national|British nationals]] such as [[British Nationals (Overseas)|British nationals (overseas)]], [[British Overseas Citizen|British overseas citizen]]s, [[British Overseas Territories Citizen|British overseas territories citizen]]s, [[British Protected Person|British protected person]]s or [[British Subjects|British subjects]] are different.

==History==
Visa requirements for British citizens were lifted by many European nations in the few years after World War II. The first changes occurred in 1947. These were removed by France on 1 January 1947.
<ref>{{cite web |url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=7823&pg=7 |title=UK Treaties Online |access-date=25 June 2017 |archive-date=25 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180725033650/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=7823&pg=7 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

This was then quickly followed by Belgium on 15 February 1947,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=6646&pg=7 |title=UK Treaties Online |access-date=25 June 2017|archive-date=29 December 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171229231951/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=6646&pg=7 |url-status=dead}}</ref> Luxembourg 15 February 1947,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=8956&pg=7 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170331115706/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=8956&pg=7 |url-status=dead |archive-date=31 March 2017 |title=UK Treaties Online}}</ref> Norway on 1 March 1947,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=9195&pg=6 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170331115325/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=9195&pg=6 |url-status=dead |archive-date=31 March 2017 |title=UK Treaties Online}}</ref> Denmark on 22 March 1947,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=7214|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170331115953/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=7214|url-status=dead|archive-date=2017-03-31|title=UK Treaties Online}}</ref> Sweden on 1 April 1947,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=10131|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170331115807/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=10131|url-status=dead|archive-date=31 March 2017|title=UK Treaties Online}}</ref> Netherlands on 15 April 1947,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=8495|title=UK Treaties Online|access-date=25 June 2017|archive-date=30 December 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171230060229/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=8495|url-status=dead}}</ref> Switzerland on 24 June 1947<ref name="to">{{cite web|url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=10251|title=UK Treaties Online|access-date=25 June 2017|archive-date=29 December 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171229231944/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=10251|url-status=dead}}</ref> Liechtenstein on 24 June 1947<ref name="to"/> and Iceland on 1 July 1947.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=10851 |title=UK Treaties Online |access-date=25 June 2017 |archive-date=29 December 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171229231928/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=10851 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

The requirement was lifted by Italy on 1 January 1948,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=8709|title=UK Treaties Online|access-date=25 June 2017|archive-date=29 December 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171229231949/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=8709|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Monaco]] (8 November 1948),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=9046|title=UK Treaties Online|access-date=25 June 2017|archive-date=29 December 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171229232038/http://treaties.fco.gov.uk/treaties/treatyrecord.htm?tid=9046|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Austria]] (15 May 1955),<ref>[http://alex.onb.ac.at/cgi-content/alex?aid=bgb&datum=19270004&seite=00001057 Austria abolished the visa requirement for British citizens on 1 August 1927] but this was reversed after the ''[[Anschluss]]'' in 1938.</ref><ref>[http://www.ris.bka.gv.at/Dokument.wxe?ResultFunctionToken=25e2faea-d00a-4bd4-a50b-7341580a09ba&Position=1&Abfrage=BgblPdf&Titel=&Bgblnummer=&SucheNachGesetzen=False&SucheNachKundmachungen=False&SucheNachVerordnungen=False&SucheNachSonstiges=False&SucheNachTeil1=False&SucheNachTeil2=False&SucheNachTeil3=False&SucheNachTeilAlt=False&VonDatum=01.01.1955&BisDatum=03.12.1955&ImRisSeit=Undefined&ResultPageSize=100&Suchworte=&Dokumentnummer=1955_161_0 Resolution of the Ministry on Internal Affairs of 28 July 1955, concerning the abolition of visas for citizens of the United States of America, the French Republic and the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland] (in German)</ref> [[Paraguay]] (27 November 1966),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mre.gov.py/tratados/public_web/DetallesTratado.aspx?id=DUAoMB0sXqHjaMW7rZu9tw==&em=bRu3GBt3aX/479zs3dcegLVjF+GtX1u/PGtpPOJXiwY=|title=ACUERDO POR NOTAS REVERSALES PARA LA SUPRESIÓN DE VISAS DE LOS PASAPORTES VÁLIDOS. REINO UNIDO |website=Paraguay Treaties Online|language=es |access-date=25 June 2017}}</ref> [[United States]] (1 July 1988), [[Poland]] (1 July 1992), [[Bulgaria]] (March 1997),<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/travel/destinations/europe/bulgaria/722234/Bulgaria-How-I-lost-my-heart-to-Sofia.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100117170418/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/travel/destinations/europe/bulgaria/722234/Bulgaria-How-I-lost-my-heart-to-Sofia.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=17 January 2010|title=Bulgaria: How I lost my heart to Sofia|first=Richard|last=Robinson|date=22 August 1997|via=The Daily Telegraph}}</ref> [[Romania]] (1 January 2001),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://193.114.50.10/travel/countryadvice.asp?RO|title=Foreign & Commonwealth Office - Travel Advice|date=26 May 2001|url-status=bot: unknown|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20010526110318/http://193.114.50.10/travel/countryadvice.asp?RO|archive-date=26 May 2001}}</ref> [[Serbia and Montenegro]] (31 May 2003),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.travelvisas.eu/visa_requirements_for_travel_to_Serbia-and-Montenegro.html|title=Serbia and Montenegro Travel Visa Requirements|website=travelvisas.eu}}</ref> [[Ukraine]] (1 May 2005),<ref>{{cite web|date=18 December 2007|title=AGREEMENT between the European Community and Ukraine on the facilitation of the issuance of visas|url=http://www.secomunidades.pt/vistos/images/docs/Ukrania%20en.pdf|access-date=18 February 2018}}</ref> [[Georgia (country)|Georgia]] (1 June 2006),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.paneuropeannetworks.com/government/commission-proposes-visa-free-travel-for-georgia/|title=Commission proposes visa-free travel for Georgia|access-date=30 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170730075144/http://www.paneuropeannetworks.com/government/commission-proposes-visa-free-travel-for-georgia/|archive-date=30 July 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Moldova]] (1 January 2007),<ref>[http://lex.justice.md/index.php?action=view&view=doc&lang=2&id=316512 Law No. 151-XVI on 8 June 2006 "On the abolition of visa regime for citizens of member States of the European Union, the United States Of America, Canada, Swiss Confederation, Kingdom of Norway, the Republic of Iceland and Japan"] (in Russian)</ref> [[Kyrgyzstan]] (27 July 2012),<ref>[http://www.mfa.gov.kg/public/images/file_library/201701240542587.docx Law of the Kyrgyz Republic On visa-free regime for citizens of some States within 60 days] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170706192220/http://mfa.gov.kg/public/images/file_library/201701240542587.docx |date=6 July 2017}} (in Russian)</ref> [[Armenia]] (10 January 2013), [[Kazakhstan]] (15 July 2014),<ref>[http://adilet.zan.kz/rus/docs/P1200000148 Resolution of the Government of the Republic of Kazakhstan on 21 January 2012 No. 148] (in Russian)</ref> [[Indonesia]] (13 June 2015),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ttgasia.com/article.php?article_id=25297|title=Finally, visa-free entry to Indonesia (TTG Asia)|access-date=30 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170730071201/http://www.ttgasia.com/article.php?article_id=25297|archive-date=30 July 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Vietnam]] (1 July 2015)<ref>Under [https://www.visa-vietnam.org/free-entry-vietnam-for-citizens-uk-france-germany-spain-and-italia Resolution No. 46/NQ-CP]</ref> [[Belarus]] (12 February 2017),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://finland.mfa.gov.by/en/embassy/news/e9d8d87b86f70f50.html|title=On the introduction of the 5 days visa-free entry to Belarus|access-date=30 July 2017|archive-date=14 October 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171014012847/http://finland.mfa.gov.by/en/embassy/news/e9d8d87b86f70f50.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Cape Verde]] (1 January 2019),<ref name="macaubusiness.com">{{cite web|url=https://www.macaubusiness.com/citizens-of-32-european-countries-exempted-from-visas-for-cape-verde-from-january-1/|title=Citizens of 32 European countries exempted from visas for Cape Verde from January 1|date=29 December 2018}}</ref> [[Uzbekistan]] (1 February 2019),<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/travel/news-and-advice/uzbekistan-visa-waiver-uk-travel-tourism-france-japan-turkey-free-silk-road-a8715911.html |title=Uzbekistan to offer visa-free travel for 45 countries - including the UK|website=[[Independent.co.uk]]|date=2019-01-07}}</ref> [[Turkey]] (2 March 2020)<ref>{{cite web|title=Türkiye'den 11 ülkeye vize muafiyeti|url=https://www.ntv.com.tr//turkiye/turkiyeden-11-ulkeye-vize-muafiyeti,fPbnHQ2Vg0O2pCqDDsQUXg|website=www.ntv.com.tr|language=tr|access-date=2020-05-12}}</ref> and [[Oman]] (December 2020).

Electronic visas for British citizens were introduced: [[India]] (15 August 2015),<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/travel/destinations/asia/india/articles/Indian-tourist-visas-e-visa-scheme-extended-to-British-travellers/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220112/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/travel/destinations/asia/india/articles/Indian-tourist-visas-e-visa-scheme-extended-to-British-travellers/ |archive-date=12 January 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Indian tourist visas: e-visa scheme extended to British travellers |first=Lizzie |last=Porter|date=5 February 2016 |via=The Daily Telegraph |newspaper=The Telegraph}}{{cbignore}}</ref> [[Djibouti]] (18 February 2018),<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.deplacementspros.com/Un-e-visa-pour-Djibouti_a47351.html |title=Un e-visa pour Djibouti |first=La |last=Redaction |date=8 March 2018}}</ref> [[Malawi]] (October 2019) and [[Mongolia]] (November 2021). In April 2021, India announced that it would stop issuing electronic visas for British citizens from August 2021, however this was reinstated in December 2022.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/india/entry-requirements |title=Entry requirements - India travel advice}}</ref>

[[Honduras]] cancelled a visa-free regime for British citizens as a reciprocal measure in August 2024.<ref>{{cite web |title=x.com |work=X (formerly Twitter) |url=https://x.com/CancilleriaHN/status/1811593980884254953 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240712044510/https://x.com/CancilleriaHN/status/1811593980884254953 |access-date=2025-05-28 |archive-date=2024-07-12}}</ref> Similarly, [[Namibia]] will introduce visas for British citizens for reciprocity reasons, starting April 2025.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://atta.travel/resource/namibia-sets-implementation-date-for-new-visa-requirements.html |title=Namibia Sets Implementation Date for New Visa Requirements |website=atta.travel}}</ref>{{Update inline|date=May 2026}}

