==Non-ordinary passports==
Holders of exclusive categories of British passports have this visa-free access, to: '''China''' <small>(diplomatic passports)</small>,<ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= CN | type= gov}}</ref> '''Kuwait''' <small>(diplomatic or official passports)</small>,<ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= KW | type= gov}}</ref> '''Mongolia''' <small>(diplomatic passports)</small>,<ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= MN| type= gov}}</ref> '''Qatar''' <small>(diplomatic or official passports and British Diplomatic Messenger or Queen's Messenger Passports)</small><ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= QA | type= gov}}</ref> and the '''United Arab Emirates''' <small>(diplomatic or official passports)</small>.<ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= AE | type= gov}}</ref><br/>Holders of diplomatic or service passports of any country have visa-free access to '''Ethiopia''',<ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= ET | type= gov}}</ref> and '''Zimbabwe'''.<ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= ZW | type= gov}}</ref> Holders of British official and diplomatic passports require a visa for '''South Africa'''.<ref>{{Timatic | nationality= GB | destination= ZA | type= gov}}</ref>

