==Travel consequences of Brexit==
{{main|Brexit}}

On 23 June 2016, a majority of the British electorate who voted, did so to leave the European Union in a [[2016 United Kingdom European Union membership referendum|nationwide referendum]].<ref>{{cite news | last1=Dzankic | first1=Jelena |title=Brexit and citizenship |url=http://eudo-citizenship.eu/news/citizenship-news/1636-brexit-and-citizenship | publisher=European Union Democracy Observatory on Citizenship |date=27 June 2016 |access-date=29 June 2016 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160820224913/http://eudo-citizenship.eu/news/citizenship-news/1636-brexit-and-citizenship|archive-date=20 August 2016 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

In March 2017, the UK sent notification of their intention to leave the EU to the European Council through Article 50 of the Lisbon Treaty. British citizens ceased to be EU citizens upon the UK's departure from the EU thus forfeiting the rights of citizens.<ref>{{cite news |title=Article 50: The simplest explanation you'll find |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/newsbeat-36634702 |access-date=29 June 2016 | publisher=BBC Newsbeat |date=27 June 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | last1=Raparel | first1=Raoul |title=The mechanics of leaving the EU – explaining Article 50 |url=http://openeurope.org.uk/today/blog/the-mechanics-of-leaving-the-eu-explaining-article-50 |website=Open Europe |access-date=29 June 2016 |date=22 February 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Article 50 TEU: Withdrawal of a Member State from the EU |url=http://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2016/577971/EPRS_BRI(2016)577971_EN.pdf |website=EuroParl | publisher=European Parliament |access-date=29 June 2016 |date=February 2016}}</ref>

The [[Brexit|UK withdrew from the EU]] on 31 January 2020, but British citizens retained the right of freedom of movement until the [[Brexit withdrawal agreement|transitional period]] ended on 31 December 2020.

From 1 January 2021, when EU law ceased to apply to the United Kingdom, British citizens are afforded visa-free visits to the [[Schengen Area]], for 90 days in any 180-day period.<ref name="ve"/><ref name="ep"/><ref name="cn"/> British citizens also enjoy visa-free entry to Bulgaria<ref>{{cite web |title=Information about brexit |url=https://www.mvr.bg/en/about-the-ministry/brexit/information-about-brexit |access-date=2020-11-26 |website=www.mvr.bg |archive-date=30 November 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201130163508/https://www.mvr.bg/en/about-the-ministry/brexit/information-about-brexit |url-status=dead}}</ref> and Romania.<ref name="fa"/>

From sometime in 2026, most visa-exempt travellers seeking entry to the EU and EEA must apply and pay for travel authorisation through [[Visa policy of the Schengen Area#ETIAS|ETIAS]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.schengenvisainfo.com/no-visa-free-traveling-brits-if-they-exit-the-eu-without-an-agreement/ |title=Brexit: No visa-free traveling for Brits if they exit the EU without an agreement |date=2018-09-17}}</ref><ref name="etiasvisa2020">{{cite web |url=https://www.etiasvisa.com/etias-news/etias-start-date-2025 |title=ETIAS Registration Will Not Become Mandatory Until 2025 |publisher=ETIAS Visa, March 2020}}</ref> This was confirmed on 12 September 2018 and has no exception, yet agreed, for British citizens.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?uri=OJ:L:2018:236:FULL&from=EN |title=Regulation (EU) 2018/1240}}</ref> This does not affect British-Irish travel which is governed by laws that pre-date the European Community.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.ontrailvisa.co.uk/news/etias-impact-uk-travelers |title=ETIAS: implications for British travellers}}</ref>

When in a non-EU country where there is no British embassy, British citizens no longer have the right to consular protection from the embassy of any other EU country present in that country.<ref>{{cite web |title=Home - Consular Protection - European Commission |url=http://ec.europa.eu/consularprotection/index.action_en |website=Consular Protection}}</ref>

==Consular protection of British citizens abroad==
[[File:Diplomatic missions of the United Kingdom.svg|thumb|800px|none|'''Diplomatic missions of the United Kingdom''']]

When in a country where there is no British embassy, British citizens may get help from the embassy of any other [[Commonwealth of Nations|commonwealth]] country present in that country. There are also informal arrangements with some other countries, including New Zealand and Australia to help British nationals in some countries.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/914039/FCO_BritsAbroad_A4web_020920.pdf |title=Support for British nationals abroad: A guide |access-date=26 November 2020 |archive-date=16 December 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201216053620/https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/914039/FCO_BritsAbroad_A4web_020920.pdf |url-status=dead}}</ref>

See also [[List of diplomatic missions of the United Kingdom]].

